  "tables": [
    {
      "label": "",
      "headers": [],
      "rows": [
        {
          "col_0": "options*object",
          "col_1": "The options object contains configuration parameters used to do initializations. If no access token or authentication callback is provided, the Initializer will fall back on an access token provided in the URL query string, or a previous access token stored in the cookie cache, if available."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "envstring",
          "col_1": "Either AutodeskProduction, AutodeskStaging, or AutodeskDevelopment. Local can be used to avoid attaching authentication headers to XHR requests."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "apistring",
          "col_1": "If automatic routing (the DS_ENDPOINTS feature flag) is enabled, must be streamingV2 for SVF2 or derivativeV2 for SVF. If automatic routing is disabled, must be streamingV2 (SVF2) or derivativeV2 (SVF) for models stored in a US data center, streamingV2_EU (SVF2) or derivativeV2_EU (SVF) for models stored in a European data center, or streamingV2_AUS (SVF2) or derivativeV2_AUS (SVF) for models stored in an Australian data center. Defaults to derivativeV2 if left undefined."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "getAccessTokenfunction",
          "col_1": "An function that provides an access token asynchronously. The function signature is getAccessToken(onSuccess), where onSuccess is a callback that getAccessToken function should invoke when a token is granted, with the token being the first input parameter for the onSuccess function, and the token expire time (in seconds) being the second input parameter for the function. Viewer relies on both getAccessToken and the expire time to automatically renew token, so it is critical that getAccessToken must be implemented as described here."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "accessTokenstring",
          "col_1": "An access token. Not needed when options.getAccessToken is provided.`"
        },
        {
          "col_0": "webGLHelpLinkstring",
          "col_1": "A link to a help page on webGL if it’s disabled."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "languagestring",
          "col_1": "Preferred language code as defined in RFC 4646, such as en, de, fr, etc. If no language is set, viewer will pick it up from the browser. If language is not as defined in RFC, viewer will fall back to “en” (English) but the behavior is undefined."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "lmvResourceRootstring",
          "col_1": "The root folder that contains LMV resources, will be derived if not specified."
        },
        {
          "col_0": "callback*function",
          "col_1": "A method the client executes when initialization is finished."
        }
      ]
    },
